    <profile name="The Pelt of the Wulfen" id="1306-e669-0160-9436" hidden="false" page="38" publicationId="0f8d-af97-3972-324c" typeId="cc8b-49d5-829c-bfaf" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Special" typeId="f917-8cd8-7592-47dd">At ranges of up to 10&quot; the Pelt of the Wulfen reduces the enemies chances of scoring a hit by -1. At 10&quot;-20&quot; the penalty is -2. At 20&quot;-30&quot; it is -3, and so on. For every 10&quot; subtract another -1. These are for shooting attacks only and are in addition to any other modifiers as well.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="The Wolf Helm of Russ" id="b549-9008-8628-2811" hidden="false" page="38" publicationId="0f8d-af97-3972-324c" typeId="cc8b-49d5-829c-bfaf" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Special" typeId="f917-8cd8-7592-47dd">Any  Space Wolf that can see the model wearing the Wolf Helm of Russ will automatically pass any Break test or psychology test they are required to take. The wearer also causes Fear.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Night Wing the Psyber Raven" id="1e2e-939b-0732-eb81" hidden="false" page="38" publicationId="0f8d-af97-3972-324c" typeId="219f-0faa-a2d8-f766" typeName="Unit">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Unit Type" typeId="49de-956f-8797-7436">Night Wing</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="M" typeId="4934-7872-3dd7-a8b6">-</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="WS" typeId="dc18-b600-96a9-a4a3">4</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="BS" typeId="f859-88a3-fdd3-b298">0</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="S" typeId="5916-04ef-0fd1-6557">3</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="T" typeId="2e7d-2383-f92f-16f9">6</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="W" typeId="ce31-f767-c572-72cc">1</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="I" typeId="a9b1-bae9-25d0-fdbf">4</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="A" typeId="e39a-b0ee-e6d1-e661">1</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="LD" typeId="c751-ec1f-edb8-fd83">-</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="The Rune Staff Stormcaller" id="e0e9-b5ed-c82f-728b" hidden="false" page="38" publicationId="0f8d-af97-3972-324c" typeId="cc8b-49d5-829c-bfaf" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Special" typeId="f917-8cd8-7592-47dd">At the start of the game deal 3 cards from the warp deck. Any force cards are retained within the rune staff, other cards are returned to the deck. Further force cards may be placed in the staff as they are dealt, up to a max of 3. During any psychic phase the force cards may be used to power the wielder&apos;s psychic abilities.
Stormcaller also adds +1 to the wielder&apos;s A and I, and adds a Strength bonus equal to its wielder&apos;s master level.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="The Hood of Gnyrll" id="07e2-2b7b-3ba8-95f8" hidden="false" page="38" publicationId="0f8d-af97-3972-324c" typeId="cc8b-49d5-829c-bfaf" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Special" typeId="f917-8cd8-7592-47dd">May be worn instead of a normal Psychic Hood. The wearer begins the battle with an additional psychic power. If his mastery level is 1, he therefore receives two psychic powers, if level 2 he receives three, if level 3 he receives four and level 4 psykers receive five.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="The Helm of Durfast" id="5ecf-6032-ac07-1a89" hidden="false" page="40" publicationId="0f8d-af97-3972-324c" typeId="cc8b-49d5-829c-bfaf" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Special" typeId="f917-8cd8-7592-47dd">If the shooter misses his target, then you may re-roll the dice again so long as your initial score is not 1. If your initial dice roll is a 1 then you may not re-reoll the dice and have missed</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="The Wulfen Stone" id="8737-4b68-c597-b70a" hidden="false" page="40" publicationId="0f8d-af97-3972-324c" typeId="cc8b-49d5-829c-bfaf" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Special" typeId="f917-8cd8-7592-47dd">Any enemy charged by the character must take a Break test as if it had sustained 25% casualties from shooting. However, instead of rolling 2D6 as normal, the enemy must roll 3D6. Daemonic foes are immune to the effect.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Hrulf&apos;s Hood of Darkness" id="56a4-f961-8192-c12c" hidden="false" page="40" publicationId="0f8d-af97-3972-324c" typeId="cc8b-49d5-829c-bfaf" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Special" typeId="f917-8cd8-7592-47dd">This can be activated at the start of the player&apos;s turn and the character model is cloaked in darkness. The model may not shoot or fight in close combat that turn, but may move up to 16&quot;. The model may not be shot at or att acked in close combat during his turn or the enemies following turn. The model is not affected by psychic powers whilst cloaked but may not use psychic powers either. It the Hood of Darkness is used for two consectuive turns or more then test to see if it fails. At the start of each turn, roll a D6. On a 4+ it fails and cannot be used again</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Torgarl&apos;s Plasma Blade" id="cd32-e764-c49f-bd0b" hidden="false" page="40" publicationId="0f8d-af97-3972-324c" typeId="d8e8-6c66-f558-30ee" typeName="Weapon">
